# launch-earth-ships-chapter.rish -- print the Claude Code loop for Incense, Pheromone, Petrichor.
#
# Three Earth ships, names seated 20260904 on Keaton's word. Unattended laps are
# Claude Code (stream-json --verbose), Darwin on the host and Linux inside
# agent-jail.sh -- the same wrap launch-claude-chapter prints. Incense is law,
# review, and captain (field GUI ~/grain; unattended loop grain-incense).
# Pheromone is the molecular star (grain-pheromone; elder furrow). Petrichor
# tends docs-geode and prose-product (grain-petrichor; elder harvest). Machines
# are doors. Each star writes in its own tree. The elder six-body charter stays
# testimony.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-earth-ships-chapter.rish
#
# THE PROMPT IS A FILE -- never a shell string. FLEET_DRY prints the command
# without opening a round or launching an agent. LOOP_LAPS=1 is the one-lap recipe.

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the durable memory lives.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the loop and the three seat prompts must exist before a hand pastes.
let loop = run ["test" "-f" "tools/f/fleet-loop.sh"]
assert loop.ok else "tools/f/fleet-loop.sh is missing"
let incense = run ["test" "-f" "tools/i/incense_seat_prompt.txt"]
assert incense.ok else "tools/i/incense_seat_prompt.txt is missing"
let pheromone = run ["test" "-f" "tools/p/pheromone_seat_prompt.txt"]
assert pheromone.ok else "tools/p/pheromone_seat_prompt.txt is missing"
let petrichor = run ["test" "-f" "tools/p/petrichor_seat_prompt.txt"]
assert petrichor.ok else "tools/p/petrichor_seat_prompt.txt is missing"

say "EARTH SHIPS -- Incense, Pheromone, Petrichor (Claude Code)"
say "=========================================================="
say ""
say "Incense is law, review, and captain. Pheromone is the molecular star."
say "Petrichor tends docs-geode (the shipping shelf -- tend, never rename)"
say "and prose-product. Machines are doors. One writer per checkout (%291)."
say "Two loops on one tree refuse; two loops on two trees is a token spend."
say "The field GUI sitting stays ~/grain (Cursor.app). Unattended laps are"
say "Claude Code. Run each loop from the tree that holds it (basename"
say "grain-incense, grain-pheromone, grain-petrichor)."
say ""
say "0) PRECONDITIONS, once per machine:"
say "   - this repo cloned with the xy remote, git submodule update --init"
say "   - claude on PATH, signed in (claude auth / login on that host)"
say "   - jq for the readable stream (brew install jq on Darwin; on NixOS,"
say "     sudo sh tools/p/pier_jq_install.sh). Without jq, raw NDJSON scrolls."
say "   - Linux also needs ai-jail (agent-jail.sh is Linux-only)"
say "   - bypass standing (once, gitignored): in .claude/settings.local.json"
say "     set permissions.defaultMode = bypassPermissions -- or keep the flag."
say "   Claude refuses --dangerously-skip-permissions as root; run as a plain user."
say "   Power is a preference, never a gate: the repo is the durable memory."
say ""
say "0b) PIER BIRTH -- all three checkouts on Host pier (Dallas), as keeper."
say "    Run from the metal clone AFTER this commit is on xy/main. Birth"
say "    never overwrites. Rewrite jail SSH paths after the mv: they pin"
say "    the old absolute directory. claude login on the pier is a"
say "    hand. Do not run the same seat on Mac and pier at once."
say ""
say "mosh pier"
say "# ssh pier   also fine"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-harvest && git pull --ff-only xy main"
say "mv /home/keeper/grain-harvest /home/keeper/grain-petrichor"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-petrichor"
say ". tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable.sh && sed_inplace 's|/home/keeper/grain-harvest|/home/keeper/grain-petrichor|g' .git/ssh_config_jail"
say "# if that file is absent, the same substitution on .git/ssh_config_urbit"
say "git config core.sshCommand 'ssh -F /home/keeper/grain-petrichor/.git/ssh_config_jail'"
say "git ls-remote xy HEAD"
say "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/b/birth_a_clone.rish /home/keeper/grain-incense"
say "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/b/birth_a_clone.rish /home/keeper/grain-pheromone"
say ""
say "    If grain-harvest is already gone, start in grain-petrichor and skip"
say "    the mv. The portable in-place helper is the pier. Birth never overwrites -- skip a dest"
say "    that already exists. After each birth, ls-remote xy from the newborn."
say "    IdentityFile often already names the field keys; core.sshCommand pins"
say "    the checkout path and must follow the mv. claude login is a hand."
say "    A pier shell may still export RYE_ZIG to grain-harvest; birth now pins"
say "    the newborn's own zig. Do not re-clone a dest that already has remotes."
say ""
say "0c) PIER RESUME -- rye bootstrap needs -lc on Linux (getpid). Dests exist."
say "    Clone, remotes, and toolchain copy already ran. Unset the leftover"
say "    harvest RYE_ZIG. Remove a leftover rye/bin/rye (bootstrap failed after"
say "    emit). Finish rye with -lc, then rishi. Birth never overwrites."
say ""
say "unset RYE_ZIG"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-incense"
say "rm -f rye/bin/rye"
say "cd rye && cp src/main.rye src/main.rye.zig && ../vendor/zig-toolchain/zig build-exe src/main.rye.zig -femit-bin=bin/rye --zig-lib-dir lib -lc && rm -f src/main.rye.zig && ./bin/rye version"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-incense"
say "mkdir -p rishi/bin"
say "env RYE_ZIG=/home/keeper/grain-incense/vendor/zig-toolchain/zig rye/bin/rye build rishi/src/main.rye -femit-bin=rishi/bin/rishi"
say "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/w/wire_lab_fn_drift_witness.rish"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-pheromone"
say "rm -f rye/bin/rye"
say "cd rye && cp src/main.rye src/main.rye.zig && ../vendor/zig-toolchain/zig build-exe src/main.rye.zig -femit-bin=bin/rye --zig-lib-dir lib -lc && rm -f src/main.rye.zig && ./bin/rye version"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-pheromone"
say "mkdir -p rishi/bin"
say "env RYE_ZIG=/home/keeper/grain-pheromone/vendor/zig-toolchain/zig rye/bin/rye build rishi/src/main.rye -femit-bin=rishi/bin/rishi"
say "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/w/wire_lab_fn_drift_witness.rish"
say ""
say "0d) MAC RENAME -- furrow becomes pheromone. Field ~/grain stays. Incense"
say "    already lives at ~/grain-incense. Do not birth grain-petrichor here"
say "    unless this Mac is meant to hold that tree too."
say ""
say "mv ~/grain-furrow ~/grain-pheromone"
say "cd ~/grain-pheromone"
say "git config core.sshCommand 'ssh -F $(pwd)/.git/ssh_config_urbit'"
say "# if ls .git/ssh_config_jail instead, point core.sshCommand at that file"
say "git ls-remote xy HEAD"
say "git pull --ff-only xy main"
say ""
say "1) SMOKE, Darwin -- host claude, same flags hush/silence use:"
say ""
say "claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max -p 'reply with exactly: pong'"
say ""
say "2) SMOKE, Linux (Host pier) -- inside the jail, launch-claude-chapter wrap:"
say ""
say "   ./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh --dangerously-skip-permissions claude --effort max -p 'reply with exactly: pong'"
say ""
say "   -p without --verbose prints nothing until the lap finishes. Silence"
say "   after the jail banner is the lap working. --verbose streams; the loop"
say "   uses --output-format stream-json --verbose so tool lines render live."
say "   Missing ai-jail is a host install (NixOS: nix profile install"
say "   github:akitaonrails/ai-jail, then AIJAIL_BIN in tools/e/enclosure.conf)."
say "   A watched lap without the jail:"
say "FLEET_BARE=1 LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh incense"
say ""
say "3) THE SEAT PROMPT is a file, tools/l/<seat>_seat_prompt.txt -- never a"
say "   shell string. FLEET_DRY prints the command; LOOP_LAPS=1 runs one lap."
say "   Elder names furrow and harvest remap, then the tree basename must"
say "   match. Round-open stashes and adopts xy/main -- do not git pull in"
say "   front of a dirty tree. After round-open the loop prints invoking"
say "   claude. Silence after that line is the API. Ctrl-C does not count"
say "   as a lap."
say ""
say "cd ~/grain-incense && FLEET_DRY=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh incense"
say "cd ~/grain-incense && LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh incense"
say "cd ~/grain-pheromone && LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh pheromone"
say "cd ~/grain-petrichor && LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh petrichor"
say ""
say "   On the pier, the same seats, those absolute paths:"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-incense && LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh incense"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-pheromone && LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh pheromone"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-petrichor && LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh petrichor"
say "cd /home/keeper/grain-incense && FLEET_BARE=1 LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh incense"
say ""
say "4) THE LOOP -- anchored to the tree that holds the script; LOOP_HOURS"
say "   bounds it (default 18). Epoch arithmetic so one spelling fits BSD and GNU."
say ""
say "cd ~/grain-incense && sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh incense"
say "cd ~/grain-pheromone && sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh pheromone"
say "cd ~/grain-petrichor && sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh petrichor"
say ""
say "5) STREAMING: the loop tees raw NDJSON to session-output/<seat>.jsonl and"
say "   rendered turns to session-output/<seat>.txt -- the read-scope law's"
say "   shared window. jq --unbuffered is the hush/silence renderer"
say "   (tools/s/stream_render.jq). Without jq, both files take the raw stream."
say ""
say "6) macOS FIELD GUI JAIL -- Cursor.app on this Mac, until Pond completes"
say "   the enclosure (gate %5). Not the unattended Claude loop. Jail-local SSH"
say "   and GPG keys already live in-tree. Launch from an ordinary terminal."
say "   --harden-home is the Rish door (GREEN on this host 20260903.234111)."
say "   --private-home through Rish hits StringTooLong on this HOME enumeration;"
say "   the bash elder still carries that flag:"
say ""
say "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cu/cursor_jail_macos.rish --harden-home"
say ""
say "   Stronger fence, bash elder, same state room:"
say "CURSOR_STATE=loops/editor-cursor ./tools/cu/cursor-jail-macos.sh --harden-home --private-home"
say ""
say "   Prove the fence any time:"
say "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cu/cursor_jail_macos_witness.rish"
say ""
say "   claude login is still a hand on each host that asks."
say ""
say "7) CUSTODY: the gates in ITINERARY stay MANUAL -- funds and keys,"
say "   provisioning and paying, the maintainer's own identity, and the"
say "   public seed. Row %387 (round-open stash vs an in-flight pass) waits"
say "   on a written policy or on Keaton's word; this loop does not take it."
say ""
say "MANY HANDS (granted 20260828, Keaton's word): a seat may spin up"
say "dependents when dividing a lap pays. Custody gates stay MANUAL, one"
say "writer per checkout (%291), and the parent answers for what they stage."
say ""
say "GREEN: Earth-ships recipe printed -- incense pheromone petrichor, doors, pier birth."
